# apex patch: report a platform WebAuthn authenticator for a desktop persona
#
# THE PROBLEM. PublicKeyCredential.isUserVerifyingPlatformAuthenticatorAvailable()
# resolves via content/browser/webauth/is_uvpaa.cc, which only implements
# content::IsUVPlatformAuthenticatorAvailable for IS_MAC (Touch ID), IS_WIN
# (WinWebAuthnApi) and IS_CHROMEOS (ChromeOSAuthenticator). A LINUX build has
# no implementation at all, so the browser always answers false -- the
# platformAuth=false tell on a persona claiming Windows/macOS (real Windows
# with Hello reports true; confirmed by the round-2 probe).
#
# THE FIX. AuthenticatorCommonImpl::IsUvpaaAvailableInternal is the single
# funnel for BOTH the JS API and the GetClientCapabilities'
# userVerifyingPlatformAuthenticator bit. When the persona claims a platform
# authenticator (APEX_FP_WEBAUTHN_PLATFORM=1), answer true at the top of the
# function -- before the request-proxy and delegate-override checks, which are
# the host's answer paths.
#
# Runtime-gated: no APEX_FP_WEBAUTHN_PLATFORM = the real (false on Linux)
# answer. The persona layer must emit it for desktop personas.
#
# Apply target: content/browser/webauth/authenticator_common_impl.cc
# (anchor edit via scripts/apply_edits.py).
--- a/content/browser/webauth/authenticator_common_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/webauth/authenticator_common_impl.cc
@@ AuthenticatorCommonImpl::IsUvpaaAvailableInternal @@
   // Serves isUserVerifyingPlatformAuthenticatorAvailable() and the
   // GetClientCapabilities platform bit; the OS-specific implementation of
   // content::IsUVPlatformAuthenticatorAvailable doesn't exist on Linux.
+  // --- apex: persona platform-authenticator ---
+  if (apex_fp::PlatformAuthenticator()) {
+    std::move(callback).Run(true);
+    return;
+  }
+  // --- end apex ---
   WebAuthenticationRequestProxy* proxy =
       GetWebAuthnRequestProxyIfActive(caller_origin);
